// Textbook-scatter schedule — single worker, no decomposition.
//
// Drives `prog.textbook.algo.nuc` (the X1' pure-kernel-call-in-index
// histogram, TASK-0430). The e2e harness selects the algorithm from this
// `schedule for` path (TASK-0049.03 per-cell algo selection) and pairs
// `kernels.textbook.rs` by the variant rule (TASK-0049.08), so an
// `08-histogram/textbook` cell compiles the textbook variant while the
// other 08 schedules keep their own algorithm variants.
//
// Single worker (`host`): the data-dependent WRITE
// `histogram[bucket(input[i])]` needs the whole of `histogram` mutable on
// one worker, which the single-worker placement trivially satisfies (no
// transfers, no cross-worker bin fan-in). The `bucket` kernel is placed
// on the same worker — it is a pure index-computing kernel called inline
// at the scatter site, not a separate decomposed stage. A DISTRIBUTED
// textbook scatter (partition the input, per-worker partial histograms,
// cross-worker element-wise-sum combine — the analog of
// `distributed.scatter.sched.nuc`) is OUT OF SCOPE for TASK-0430 and is
// the filed broaden follow-up TASK-0432. Output is bit-identical to
// 08-histogram/naive,
// 08-histogram/scatter, and reference.bin.

schedule for "../prog.textbook.algo.nuc" {
    workers = { host };

    place load_input  on host;
    place save_output on host;
    place bucket      on host;
    place inc         on host;

    // No loop transforms, no transfer directives (single worker).
}
